From 15c5316ce343036c610ee96c901bd5f08d0a8b13 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Nucleon Dev <dev@localhost>
Date: Mon, 26 Oct 2026 01:48:33 +1100
Subject: [PATCH] feat(client): show MCP-UI cards by default in tool calls

A tool call whose attachments carry a renderable MCP-UI resource (text/html
ui_resources) now opens by default, and the group containing it no longer
auto-collapses over it. The card renders first; the raw tool output moves
behind a collapsed "Output" disclosure, then Parameters. Calls without a
card, the global autoExpandTools preference, the iframe sandbox, the
renderer and onUIAction handling are unchanged.

- MCPUIResource/supported.ts: isSupportedUIResource + getSupportedUIResources
- ToolCall: open when a card is present; reveal once on late arrival
- ToolCallGroup: no auto-collapse with a card; reveal once on late arrival
- ToolCallInfo: card-first layout with Output disclosure
- tests: unit + real-renderer integration (sandbox attr, caveat in srcdoc)

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
